2026-07-27  Bob Friesenhahn  <bfriesen@simple.dallas.tx.us>

        * magick/xwindow.c (MagickXImportImage): Avoid heap buffer
        overflow of image filename field if X11 window name is longer than
        MaxTextExtent-1.  Addresses ImageMagick CVE-2026-61464
        (GHSA-76q6-2p6h-xjqr). In order to exploit this, the attacker must
        have access to the X11 display, would need to set an X11 window
        title with text longer than 2052 bytes (e.g. use 'xdotool
        selectwindow set_window --name FOO', execute 'gm import x:', guide
        the mouse cursor to the window, and click in it, or use '-window
        id' where 'id' is the identity of the window to be imported (e.g.
        reported by 'xwininfo'). If this issue is exploitable, then the
        system has much more serious issues.  Issue was reported to me via
        an email from Petr Gajdos on July 27, 2026.

